  "compatibilityNotes": [
    "After fresh/identity admission, run exact S canonical --table vault_keys, only the three pinned legacy CREATE TABLE fragments, then unchanged canonical --init and the reviewed overlays. Do not execute the full legacy/local SQL.",
    "Legacy public.users is absent in the observed UAT metadata and is not required by the source prod_core_schema. Do not invent a users table or use db/local/bootstrap_base_schema.sql.",
    "The source initializer creates request_id as VARCHAR(32); canonical migration 093 changes it to TEXT, matching the observed metadata.",
    "Observed metadata JSONB default is {}. The source initializer allows NULL and has no default. Preserve canonical source semantics; do not import observed defaults as arbitrary DDL.",
    "The three finite global catalogs and 24 source-authored public SEC discovery profiles are separately classified. Exact pinned stable identities/values are checked; no arbitrary nonempty owner/event/credential/outbox rows are admitted.",
    "The metadata artifact is schema-only historical evidence, not current UAT, application, image, production or environment acceptance.",
    "The fixed qualification initializer executes the real source through370, then only immutable344 overlays407,408,418,419,423. 407 is outside a transaction; no overlay ledger receipts are fabricated. Cluster identity pins come from read-only DEV/UAT evidence; current server identity and PostgreSQL major are checked before DDL. The observed minor version is provenance, not permission to change target."
